Key facts from the window:
- The store route is pushed at 18:26:35.528 / params logged 18:26:36.031, BEFORE
  /api/v1/config returns 200 at 18:26:36.557.
- NO GET /api/v1/stores/details/... ever fired in this run. The store-details
  fetch never started, so StoreLoadFailureView (the widget this ticket changed)
  had not been built and could not be reached: it renders only after a fetch
  resolves store == null && !isLoading.
- Flutter printed no ErrorWidget stack to logcat (tag `flutter` or *:E) — the
  message was only on the red ErrorWidget surface. Validity: 21 flutter lines in
  the window, 0 lines matching FAIL|ERR|Exception|#0.

Why this is NOT attributable to NEARS-1603:
- The two UserApp files this diff touches are
  lib/features/store/widgets/store_load_failure_view.dart and
  lib/common/widgets/dls/nears_error_retry.dart. Neither contains a `!`
  null-assertion; the only `!` in the delegate chain is `subtitle!` inside an
  `if (subtitle != null)` guard in NEmptyState (unchanged by this diff).
- store_screen.dart, which does dereference
  Get.find<SplashController>().configModel!.moduleConfig!.module!... , is NOT in
  the diff.

